{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8c1f0a6e-4d2b-4a17-9f3c-templateupdate01",
    "name": "Template Update Advisor API",
    "description": "Workflow and validations for the Template Update Advisor (Caseware take-home, Part 2).\n\n## Before you run\n\n1. `docker compose up -d` \u2014 starts PostgreSQL on :5433\n2. `mvn spring-boot:run` \u2014 Flyway migrates on startup\n3. Seed the projection (it is normally fed by events from the engagement management system, which is outside this slice):\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO engagement_template_state\n  (engagement_id, template_id, current_version, declined_versions)\nVALUES ('eng-1','audit-ca',3,'{4}'),\n       ('eng-2','audit-ca',5,'{}'),\n       ('eng-3','audit-ca',6,'{}')\nON CONFLICT (engagement_id) DO NOTHING;\n```\n\nRun it with:\n```\ndocker exec -i advisor-postgres psql -U advisor -d advisor\n```\n\n## The scenario these tests encode\n\n| Engagement | On version | Declined | With v6 published |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `eng-1` | v3 | v4 | pending, **v3 \u2192 v6** |\n| `eng-2` | v5 | \u2014 | pending, v5 \u2192 v6 |\n| `eng-3` | v6 | \u2014 | omitted, already current |\n\n`eng-1` is the case worth watching. It declined v4, but its pending range still starts at **v3** \u2014 declining defers a version, it does not skip its content. That rule is asserted directly in the *Domain invariants* folder.\n\n## Running order\n\nFolders are ordered as a workflow and are meant to run top to bottom (Postman Runner, or `newman run postman/template-update-advisor.postman_collection.json`). *Preconditions* fails fast with an actionable message if the app is down or the projection is unseeded.\n\n## Known limitation\n\n`firmId` in the path is accepted but not yet used to select a tenant \u2014 the slice runs against a single schema, and multi-tenancy is by schema-per-firm in the design. Any `firmId` returns the same rows.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Preconditions",
      "description": "Run first. Fails loudly and specifically when the environment is not ready.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health \u2014 app is up and the database is reachable",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Port {{baseUrl}} is actually the Template Update Advisor', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body, 'no JSON body - something else is serving this port').to.not.be.null;",
                  "    pm.expect(body, 'expected an Actuator health payload. Another process may hold this port: '",
                  "        + 'check with `lsof -nP -iTCP:8080 -sTCP:LISTEN`').to.have.property('status');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Application reports UP', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('UP'));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('PostgreSQL is connected (Flyway will have migrated on startup)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.components.db.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.components.db.details.database).to.eql('PostgreSQL');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
